{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-22T01:53:53.106Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8fcf1176eceedef40be11ce4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-998juj","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","lineage:pm-xp7ldt","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-998juj+pm-xp7ldt+pm-zi34i1","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-998juj","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","lineage:pm-xp7ldt","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-22T01:53:53.105Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implemented on branch fix/sdk-admission-scope-identity. The scope store in src/sdk/runtime.ts is now a record of the physical tracker root (realpath, or the resolved spelling before the directory exists) and the activated runtime, instead of a boolean. One helper, runUnderOpenExtensionScope, decides every nested entry: runAction, runWithActiveExtensions without its own cwd, runInActiveExtensionScope and the PmClient item-transaction context. Same root: the scope is reused and the nested call receives the activated runtime, so a nested extension action dispatches (before, a nested dispatch got no runtime and answered 'Unsupported native pm action'). Another root: that tracker's extensions are activated in fresh request-local registries under the gate slot the open scope already holds, and the caller's registrations are back when the nested call returns. runAction now publishes the scope its dispatch holds, which removes the wait described in the second comment: a command dispatched with an explicit cwd can call runInActiveExtensionScope, runWithActiveExtensions and a nested runAction for its tracker. A nested disabled scope is bound to the root it names. Left as documented behaviour: a nested runWithActiveExtensions that passes its own cwd still asks for exclusive use of the process working directory. Proof: tests/unit/sdk/extension/scope-tracker-identity.spec.ts (4 cases); all four fail on the previous runtime, two of them by timing out on the activation gate."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-22T01:53:53.106Z"}],"before_hash":"11898ca4edbbe0e3f21d59a3bb41adb479417864a043c01fd4a32250a431c6a3","after_hash":"84be1d08e89445078b2147f2b7d5e34fb5cd8ea38d07fd78275c90c8ba42f1f5","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5095f2dc08815ebd027336ef36a8534de18cd7850e98d1896f4405619130c76f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-22T02:20:49.482Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8fcf1176eceedef40be11ce4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-998juj","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","lineage:pm-xp7ldt","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-998juj+pm-xp7ldt+pm-zi34i1","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-998juj","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","lineage:pm-xp7ldt","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"tests_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-22T02:20:49.482Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tests","value":[{"command":"node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/sdk/extension/scope-tracker-identity.spec.ts","scope":"project","provenance":{"author":"harness:claude-code","created_at":"2026-11-22T02:20:49.430Z","source_kind":"local_mutation","source_ref":"fix/sdk-admission-scope-identity"}}]}],"before_hash":"84be1d08e89445078b2147f2b7d5e34fb5cd8ea38d07fd78275c90c8ba42f1f5","after_hash":"4eae63ec85bdddb4dc4cb06e2f87f7e278a7c6f4655abcda0b220ce841e7e11b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f65ceb50953f4cbe6f4358e1ce3e1c0aa7adab7aa09dc07bc297019b4fdd9468"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-22T03:03:50.093Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8fcf1176eceedef40be11ce4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-l6wdvh","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","release:pm-998juj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-l6wdvh+pm-xp7ldt+pm-zi34i1","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-l6wdvh","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","release:pm-998juj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-22T03:03:50.093Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"First Codex review (gpt-6.2-sol, xhigh) of the branch, findings on the scope change, each verified and fixed in the follow-up commit. (1) An AsyncLocalStorage scope record stays visible to timers and promises its callback left behind, after the gate slot is released: the record now carries a live flag that is cleared when the callback settles, and an expired scope is treated as absent. (2) A nested call with noExtensions under the scope's own tracker inherited the caller's extensions once runAction published its scope: it now runs in empty registries. (3) A nested runAction with an explicit cwd resolved the tracker from that directory but never entered it: a cwd other than the current directory is refused with reason nested_cwd_unavailable, for runAction and runWithActiveExtensions alike, which also replaces the wait documented in the previous comment. (4) With a relative cwd and a relative path, the scope recorded one tracker and activation (after chdir) resolved another: the cwd is resolved to an absolute path once and the resolved root is the one activated. (5) The PmClient preview path activated another tracker outside the configuration-only settings wrapper: nested activation now runs inside it. The spec grew to 7 cases."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-22T03:03:50.093Z"}],"before_hash":"4eae63ec85bdddb4dc4cb06e2f87f7e278a7c6f4655abcda0b220ce841e7e11b","after_hash":"357cb45ff9e119400faa6976b8ebd37a64545c9e71c3fe7a172c88067a995a5a","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"dac7afc0c6c75bfebe7a0b9b604793cab488d2f05fb7d8a4f80585d7e24e4414"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-22T03:21:44.890Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8fcf1176eceedef40be11ce4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-l6wdvh","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","release:pm-998juj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-l6wdvh+pm-xp7ldt+pm-zi34i1","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-l6wdvh","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","release:pm-998juj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-22T03:21:44.890Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Second Codex round on the scope change, verified and fixed. A callback bound inside a nested scope and resumed after that scope settled queued for the gate behind its own live ancestor (an explicit-cwd outer scope holds the exclusive slot): scope records now link to their parent, and resumed work runs under the nearest live ancestor's slot with a fresh activation, never with the settled scope's registries. While another tracker's extensions activated, the context still advertised the caller's scope although the registries were already the nested ones, so an activate() callback writing to the caller's tracker ran unguarded: the nested scope is now published for its tracker before its extensions load. A relative cwd was resolved at entry but the original string was passed to chdir: the captured absolute directory is used. PmClient transaction methods apply the same nested cwd refusal. Declined with reason: keeping the gate slot until un-awaited nested work finishes. Work a callback starts and does not await has left every scope by definition; docs/SDK.md now states that nested work must be awaited."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-22T03:21:44.890Z"}],"before_hash":"357cb45ff9e119400faa6976b8ebd37a64545c9e71c3fe7a172c88067a995a5a","after_hash":"e2b8968520aa16388933f254b8f4c29ae95211c046aa3cb594754a512b7f7223","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"577c543029850cbcbc47a53cdebb25db5713eb9c054f46bf5e214fd410bfa481"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-22T03:22:39.267Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8fcf1176eceedef40be11ce4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-l6wdvh","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","release:pm-998juj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-l6wdvh+pm-xp7ldt+pm-zi34i1","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-l6wdvh","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","release:pm-998juj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-22T03:22:39.267Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/contract_change","value":{"api":"runAction, runWithActiveExtensions, runInActiveExtensionScope, PmClient item-transaction methods (nested calls inside an open extension scope)","before":"Any nested call reused the open scope whatever tracker it addressed, ignored a nested noExtensions and a nested cwd in runAction, and a nested runWithActiveExtensions with its own cwd waited for the activation gate","after":"A nested call for another tracker activates that tracker in request-local registries; a nested noExtensions call runs in empty registries; a nested cwd other than the current directory is refused with reason nested_cwd_unavailable; runAction publishes its scope, so nested same-tracker work reuses it and a nested extension action dispatches; a scope ends when its callback settles","migrate":"Inside a scope address a tracker with path instead of cwd. A host that relied on tracker A registrations judging tracker B writes must install the guard in tracker B. Await nested work inside the callback that started it"}}],"before_hash":"e2b8968520aa16388933f254b8f4c29ae95211c046aa3cb594754a512b7f7223","after_hash":"5b7e350d6506f159fee5c935fc2d8a39d8ee2ec990ed2407851fa6ecbd675a0a","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"06c21919bba097bbe0789241cb66916fa1d4dd50238333d4e9386dedac2d1ab6"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-22T03:40:38.653Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8fcf1176eceedef40be11ce4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-l6wdvh","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","release:pm-998juj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-l6wdvh+pm-xp7ldt+pm-zi34i1","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-l6wdvh","claim:pm-xp7ldt","claim:pm-zi34i1","release:pm-998juj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-22T03:40:38.652Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Third Codex round, verified and fixed. An injected extension-host client took the host shortcut before the tracker check, so context.sdk.client.run with a path override wrote to another tracker under the host's guards: the shortcut now applies to the host's own tracker only, and another tracker is activated like any nested call. Inside a nested activation, an activate() or deactivate() callback addressing its own tracker matched the placeholder scope and ran with empty registries: the placeholder is marked not ready and such a call is refused with reason extension_scope_not_ready. Review ended after three rounds: each round's findings were narrower than the last, and the remaining surface is covered by 10 spec cases."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-22T03:40:38.653Z"}],"before_hash":"5b7e350d6506f159fee5c935fc2d8a39d8ee2ec990ed2407851fa6ecbd675a0a","after_hash":"df9c8c268ccf0f2c00fd7ad2070cb682fcfb462ecc9f03558fcddb0050503987","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e7622c7f7db7844bc699347ba4796efa25d4071ca16b7777d651b60d7f9d8ec2"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-22T09:29:02.174Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ab4bb49999c22e44f166c80b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-jvb9pk","lineage:pm-jvb9pk","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-jvb9pk","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-jvb9pk","lineage:pm-jvb9pk","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-22T09:29:02.174Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round on head 7e0844634 (Greptile P1, src/sdk/runtime.ts host shortcut). An injected host client took the shared-registration shortcut whenever the nearest live scope had its tracker's root. A callback captured inside an awaited scope for tracker B and awaited after B settled reaches A's live scope through the settled child, but its context carries B's cleared registries, so the host write for A ran with no guards. The shortcut now also requires the live scope to be the context's own store (hostSharesOpenRegistrations); otherwise the call goes through runUnderOpenExtensionScope, which activates A again under the ancestor's slot. Spec: scope-tracker-identity.spec.ts, \"judges a host client's write resumed from a settled nested scope with a fresh activation of its tracker\" (activations alpha, beta, alpha; refusal alpha_denied).\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-22T09:29:02.174Z"}],"before_hash":"df9c8c268ccf0f2c00fd7ad2070cb682fcfb462ecc9f03558fcddb0050503987","after_hash":"6d0b5c2e1b7af799e6ed8282e9c5